 "notes": "Stretch 1. p.105: started below the rule under 'Ani em maāχeru'. Overlines (rubric): XLIV title — long overline over Re en temt mit em nem (ends after nem; 'em Neter-χert' not under it), second short overline over t'eṭ àn only. XLV title p.106 row 4: overline from Re to just past the owl of em (em counted rubric; Neter-χert not), then short overline over t'eṭ àn. p.107 row 3: overline begins over àr and runs to the end of the row (àr reχ re pen àn) and continues on row 4 over ḥua-f em (ends at the owl); Neter-χert Àusàr not. XLVI title p.107 row 5: overline over Re en temt sekt unen ānχu (ends after ānχu; em Neter-χert not); row 6 short overline over t'eṭ àn. Line numerals — XLIV: 1. at start of title (p.105 row 1); 2. before em (p.105 row 3); 3. inside àmen - nuà between det and N35 (p.105 row 4) — word kept in line 2; 4. after un, before àu (p.105 row 5); 5. inside χem - à - tu between A1 and X1 (p.105 row 6) — word kept in line 4; 6. inside maa - [à] between U1 and the vultures (p.106 row 2) — word kept in line 5. XLV: 1. at start of title (p.106 row 4); 2. inside urṭ between D46 and the det (p.107 row 1); 3. inside urṭ - s[et] (p.107 row 2); 4. inside àru - nà between Z1 and N35 (p.107 row 3). XLVI: 1. at start of title (p.107 row 5); 2. after à 'Hail', before ḥunnu (p.107 row 6). p.108 rows 1–2 carry no numeral (line 2 continues); stopped at the rule after 'unun Àusàr'. Raised ¹ after 'netherworld.' (p.106 row 3 English) and after the Neter-χert group (p.107 row 5) are footnote marks. Brackets in transliteration only ('s[et]' three times on p.107 rows 2) are not hieroglyph restorations. 'sep sen' treated as one word each time (two signs, one gloss). Gloss for 'àu àpt(?) à em' aligned positionally: '[My] brow [is like that] of'."
